    <string name="ob1_title">Smooth games, normal battery</string>
    <string name="ob1_body">HyperOS caps many games at 60Hz. Hyper120 removes that cap only for the games you choose. Everything else keeps adaptive refresh, so battery life stays the same. No root, no PC.</string>
    <string name="ob2_title">Every game has its own limit</string>
    <string name="ob2_body">Hyper120 unlocks the screen, but a game still decides how many frames it draws. Some never go above 60. Others only offer 120 in their own settings, often only on phones the developer has approved. Look for these tags in the app list:</string>
    <string name="ob2_tag120">Can go above 60. Turn it on in the game\'s graphics settings.</string>
    <string name="ob2_tag90">Can go up to 90.</string>
    <string name="ob2_tag60">The game stops at 60. Nothing can make it faster.</string>
    <string name="ob3_title">Keep it running</string>
    <string name="ob3_body">HyperOS closes background apps aggressively. Do these steps so Hyper120 keeps working after you leave the app.</string>
    <string name="ob3_battery">1. Battery saver: No restrictions</string>
    <string name="ob3_battery_done">✓ Battery limits removed</string>
    <string name="ob3_battery_hint">Opens App info. Tap Battery saver and choose No restrictions.</string>
    <string name="ob3_autostart">2. Allow Autostart</string>
    <string name="ob3_autostart_hint">Find Hyper120 in the list and switch it on.</string>

